<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  ===========================================================================
  THIS REGISTRATION HAS TO BE IN `frontend`, NOT GLOBAL
  ===========================================================================
  It lived in etc/di.xml and was never invoked. The symptom was severe and
  looked like something else entirely: a shopper chose InstaPay, the order was
  created (POST /rest/ar/V1/carts/mine/payment-information -> 200), and then
  they were sent to the success page instead of the transfer page, so the
  receipt was never collected and the order sat in pending_payment unpaid.

  Diagnosed by elimination on the live store, after the class itself was
  confirmed correct, deployed, DI-compiled and cache-flushed:

    - `transferUrl` appeared NOWHERE in a fresh 297KB checkout page.
    - The module was demonstrably enabled and etc/di.xml demonstrably read —
      SpartrakInstaPayFacade is declared in that same file and the payment
      method rendered in the checkout.
    - The two Spartrak providers that DO reach window.checkoutConfig —
      Spartrak_Payment and Spartrak_PickupLocation — differ from this one in
      exactly one respect: they register in etc/frontend/di.xml.

  Magento composes DI per AREA: the area configuration is merged over the
  global one, and for a repeated type+argument pair the area's value REPLACES
  the global array rather than deep-merging its items. So the moment any
  frontend di.xml declared `configProviders` on CompositeConfigProvider, this
  module's global entry stopped existing in the frontend area — with no error,
  because nothing is missing from Magento's point of view.

  Registering in the same area as the other contributors puts this item in the
  same merge and it survives.

  It belongs in `frontend` on its own merits anyway: window.checkoutConfig is a
  rendered-page concern, which is the reasoning Spartrak_Payment's own
  etc/frontend/di.xml already records.
-->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:ObjectManager/etc/config.xsd">
    <type name="Magento\Checkout\Model\CompositeConfigProvider">
        <arguments>
            <argument name="configProviders" xsi:type="array">
                <item name="spartrak_instapay" xsi:type="object">
                    Spartrak\InstaPay\Model\Ui\ConfigProvider
                </item>
            </argument>
        </arguments>
    </type>
</config>
